 {"key": "analysis.hilbertSharpQuadraticCorrectorBound", "local_decl": "AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Analysis.HilbertCorrectorBound.quadratic_corrector_bound_of_square_identity", "local_file": "AutoSamplingTheory/TechnicalLemmas/Analysis/HilbertCorrectorBound.lean", "status": "formalized-local", "sald_use": "PBPS consumer; no SALD change", "tags": ["Hilbert", "selfadjoint", "quadratic-form", "sharp-corrector"], "upstream_decl": "Sharp quadratic corrector bound from a selfadjoint square identity", "upstream_file": "arXiv2609.06905v1 Appendix B3 (B23); ASTIS auxiliary Hilbert-space estimate", "verified_commit": "3ad3b127b5a645be9cf71b3d14520b2d8fea3122", "evidence": "runs/20261007-companion-priority/pbps-sharp-energy68/verified.json", "next_action": "Independently exact-science68 VERIFIED 3ad3b127b5a645be9cf71b3d14520b2d8fea3122. Arbitrary complete real Hilbert space including zero: selfadjoint K,D, I+K²=D² and norm(D)<=c with c>=0 yield the exact c/2 two-component bound. Uses the sum of squared component norms. No c>=1, finite dimension, nontriviality, operator positivity or K,D commutation premise. Actual PBPS supplies D=Inv and K=A0 Inv. Not a separately printed paper theorem."}
